{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "package": "Python",
  "installation_title": "Installation of Python 3",
  "contents_title": "Contents of Python 3",
  "installed_labels": {
    "programs": "Installed programs",
    "libraries": "Installed library",
    "directories": "Installed directories"
  },
  "installation_blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "First, apply a patch for compatibility with OpenSSL 4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Prepare Python for compilation:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "definition-list",
      "title": "The meaning of the configure options:",
      "items": [
        {
          "term_content": [
            {
              "type": "parameter",
              "text": "--with-system-expat"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This switch enables linking against the system version of"
                },
                {
                  "type": "application",
                  "text": "Expat"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "term_content": [
            {
              "type": "parameter",
              "text": "--enable-optimizations"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "This switch enables extensive, but time-consuming, optimization steps. The interpreter is built twice; tests performed on the first build are used to improve the optimized final version."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Compile the package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 2
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Some tests are known to occasionally hang indefinitely. So to test the results, run the test suite but set a 2-minute time limit for each test case:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "For a relatively slow system you may need to increase the time limit and 1 SBU (measured when building Binutils pass 1 with one CPU core) should be enough. Some tests are flaky, so the test suite will automatically re-run failed tests. If a test failed but then passed when re-run, it should be considered as passed."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Two tests,"
        },
        {
          "type": "literal",
          "text": "test_urllib2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "and"
        },
        {
          "type": "literal",
          "text": "test_urllibnet"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", are known to fail because name resolution is not configured in the incomplete LFS environment."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Install the package:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 4
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We use the"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "command to install Python 3 programs and modules for all users as"
        },
        {
          "type": "systemitem",
          "text": "root"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "in several places in this book. This conflicts with the Python developers' recommendation: to install packages into a virtual environment, or into the home directory of a regular user (by running"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "as this user). A multi-line warning is triggered whenever"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "is issued by the"
        },
        {
          "type": "systemitem",
          "text": "root"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "user."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The main reason for the recommendation is to avoid conflicts with the system's package manager ("
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "dpkg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", for example). LFS does not have a system-wide package manager, so this is not a problem. Also,"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "will check for a new version of itself whenever it's run. Since domain name resolution is not yet configured in the LFS chroot environment,"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "cannot check for a new version of itself, and will produce a warning."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After we boot the LFS system and set up a network connection, a different warning will be issued, telling the user to update"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "from a pre-built wheel on PyPI (whenever a new version is available). But LFS considers"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "to be a part of Python 3, so it should not be updated separately. Also, an update from a pre-built wheel would deviate from our objective: to build a Linux system from source code. So the warning about a new version of"
        },
        {
          "type": "command",
          "text": "pip3"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "should be ignored as well. If you wish, you can suppress all these warnings by running the following command, which creates a configuration file:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "kind": "important",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In LFS and BLFS we normally build and install Python modules with the"
            },
            {
              "type": "command",
              "text": "pip3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "command. Please be sure that the"
            },
            {
              "type": "command",
              "text": "pip3 install"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "commands in both books are run as the"
            },
            {
              "type": "systemitem",
              "text": "root"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "user (unless it's for a Python virtual environment). Running"
            },
            {
              "type": "command",
              "text": "pip3 install"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "as a non-"
            },
            {
              "type": "systemitem",
              "text": "root"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "user may seem to work, but it will cause the installed module to be inaccessible by other users."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "command",
              "text": "pip3 install"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "will not reinstall an already installed module automatically. When using the"
            },
            {
              "type": "command",
              "text": "pip3 install"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "command to upgrade a module (for example, from meson-0.61.3 to meson-0.62.0), insert the option"
            },
            {
              "type": "parameter",
              "text": "--upgrade"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "into the command line. If it's really necessary to downgrade a module, or reinstall the same version for some reason, insert"
            },
            {
              "type": "parameter",
              "text": "--force-reinstall --no-deps"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "into the command line."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If desired, install the preformatted documentation:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "command",
      "command_index": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "definition-list",
      "title": "The meaning of the documentation install commands:",
      "items": [
        {
          "term_content": [
            {
              "type": "option",
              "text": "--no-same-owner"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "and"
            },
            {
              "type": "option",
              "text": "--no-same-permissions"
            }
          ],
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Ensure the installed files have the correct ownership and permissions. Without these options,"
                },
                {
                  "type": "application",
                  "text": "tar"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "will install the package files with the upstream creator's values."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
